+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+//
+// DADAO frame lowering for M3 (LLVM-038t, ADR-0018 C7/C8).
+//
+// Frame layout (StackGrowsDown, LocalAreaOffset = 0):
+//   entry SP ─┬─ [FP]          rbfp = rb63 (only when hasFP)
+//             │  [saved FP]    fixed slot at -8 (only when hasFP)
+//             │  locals / spill slots
+//   current SP┴─
+//
+// Prologue (SP-only):  add.si rbsp, -StackSize
+// Prologue (FP):       st.o rbfp, [rbsp, -8]      ; save the caller's FP
+//                      add.si rbsp, -StackSize    ; allocate the frame
+//                      rb2rb rbfp, rbsp           ; rbfp = entry SP
+//                      add.si rbfp, StackSize
+// Epilogue (SP-only):  add.si rbsp, +StackSize
+// Epilogue (FP):       rb2rb rbsp, rbfp           ; rbsp = entry SP
+//                      ld.o rbfp, [rbsp, -8]      ; restore the caller's FP
+//
+// Callee-saved register sets (CSR) are LLVM-039t; only the frame pointer is
+// saved here (rb63, conditionally reserved — see DADAORegisterInfo).
+//
+// Large-frame addressing (ADR-0018 C7 D4, rev. 2026-10-08; LLVM-064t) is
+// cost-driven, with four forms selected by the compiler (all in
+// DADAORegisterInfo::eliminateFrameIndex):
+//   ① [sp, disp12]                         |disp| <= 2047
+//   ② rb2rb tmp, sp ; add.si tmp, N ; [tmp, 0]        |N| <= 128K
+//   ③ set.zw/or.w tmpRD, N ; add.o tmpRB, sp, tmpRD ; [tmpRB, 0]   any N
+//   ④ ldm/stm {..}, [sp, tmp]              immu6 = 1 single / >1 batch
+// Form ①/②/③ cover a single access; the batch case (form ④) is the
+// callee-saved save.  This makes any frame size reachable (ISS-138).
+//
+// INVARIANT (contract-isa.md §15.1, rule `mreg_range_overflow`): an
+// `ldm.*`/`stm.*` immediate encodes a contiguous register range with the hard
+// rule `start + immu6 <= 64` (no wrap / truncation).  rb63 is the highest RB
+// number, so it may only be the *last* element (or a singleton) of a batch
+// range; {rb32..rb63} (start 32 + immu6 32 = 64) is legal.  Project convention
+// (contract-abi.md §1.3): rb63 = FP is saved to its own dedicated slot
+// (`st.o rb63, [sp, -8]` in emitPrologue); a batch callee-saved save normally
+// does not include it, and if it did it would have to sit at the range END.
+// emitCalleeSavedRegs keeps rb63-as-run-top as the separate offset holder, so
+// it is never a range start.
+//
+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
